# madcide status-line format (IDE-9a) — JOE's joerc vocabulary, shipped
# with joerc's own default strings. lmsg renders left-justified, rmsg
# right-justified; rmsg's FIRST character (after "rmsg ") is the FILL
# between the two halves.
#
# Supported seats today: %n name · %m "(Modified) " · %R "(Read only) "
# · %r row / %c col (digits width-pad: %4r) · %o byte offset · %k the
# pending chord (chord echo) · %x the enclosing context (madcide renders
# its AST-backed enclosing function here — exact where JOE's is a
# textual backward heuristic) · %y the active VIEW name in JOE's
# "(syntax)" seat · %% a literal percent.
#
# Unsupported joerc escapes render EMPTY and light up as their features
# land (%T overtype, %W wordwrap, %I autoindent, %X rectangle, %M macro,
# %S shell, ...). \i..\l attribute escapes are consumed — the row
# renders inverse whole-line; intra-line styling is a named seat.
lmsg \i%k%T%W%I%X %n %m%y%R %M %x
rmsg  %S Row %4r Col %3c
